invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_sp1 returns without the wipe below its body, so the two
  primes' records, the message, both halves and the candidate stay in the
  stack, and a candidate that failed its check factors the modulus.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test requires no two words of a value the call held
  in the stack below it, and requires the stack equal under two secrets
  (docs/decisions.md 181).

--- old
    int verified = sign_halves(cpu, k, em, sig);
    rsa_sign64_wipe_below();
--- new
    int verified = sign_halves(cpu, k, em, sig);
